pe-theory/releases/download/v1.0/main.pdf","relatedIdentifierType":"URL"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.1145/3437992.3439919","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"https://isa-afp.org/entries/Padic_Field.html","relatedIdentifierType":"URL"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.4230/LIPIcs.ITP.2022.14","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.1007/978-3-319-21401-6_26","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.1007/BFb0079065","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.1145/3293880.3294089","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"https://math-comp.github.io/mcb/","relatedIdentifierType":"URL"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.1145/3372885.3373824","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"arXiv:2207.09486","relatedIdentifierType":"arXiv"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.2478/forma-2014-0024","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.1017/S0960129514000541","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.2478/forma-2020-0022","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.2478/forma-2022-0022","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.2478/forma-2021-0004","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.4230/LIPIcs.ITP.2021.18","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[{"number":"13","titles":[{"title":"LIPIcs, Volume 268, ITP 2023"},{"title":"14th International Conference on Interactive Theorem Proving (ITP 2023)","titleType":"Subtitle"}],"volume":"268","lastPage":"13:18","firstPage":"13:1","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl – Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","contributors":[{"name":"Naumowicz, Adam","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Adam","familyName":"Naumowicz","contributorType":"Editor"},{"name":"Thiemann, René","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"René","familyName":"Thiemann","contributorType":"Editor"}],"relationType":"IsPublishedIn","publicationYear":"2023","relatedItemType":"ConferenceProceeding","relatedItemIdentifier":{"relatedItemIdentifier":"10.4230/LIPIcs.ITP.2023","relatedItemIdentifierType":"DOI"}},{"titles":[{"title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs)"}],"volume":"268","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl – Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik","relationType":"IsPublishedIn","publicationYear":"2023","relatedItemType":"Collection","relatedItemIdentifier":{"relatedItemIdentifier":"1868-8969","relatedItemIdentifierType":"ISSN"}}],"sizes":["18 pages","810987 bytes"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"version":null,"rightsList":[{"lang":"en","rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","rightsIdentifier":"cc by 4.0"},{"rights":"info:eu-repo/semantics/openAccess"}],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","description":"The field ℝ of real numbers is obtained from the rational numbers ℚ by taking the completion with respect to the usual absolute value. We then define the complex numbers ℂ as an algebraic closure of ℝ. The p-adic analogue of the real numbers is the field ℚ_p of p-adic numbers, obtained by completing ℚ with respect to the p-adic norm. In this paper, we formalize in Lean 3 the definition of the p-adic analogue of the complex numbers, which is the field ℂ_p of p-adic complex numbers, a field extension of ℚ_p which is both algebraically closed and complete with respect to the extension of the p-adic norm.\r\nMore generally, given a field K complete with respect to a nonarchimedean real-valued norm, and an algebraic field extension L/K, we show that there is a unique norm on L extending the given norm on K, with an explicit description.\r\nBuilding on the definition of ℂ_p, we formalize the definition of the Fontaine period ring B_{HT} and discuss some applications to the theory of Galois representations and to p-adic Hodge theory.\r\nThe results formalized in this paper are a prerequisite to formalize Local Class Field Theory, which is a fundamental ingredient of the proof of Fermat’s Last Theorem.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"lang":"en","description":"LIPIcs, Vol. 268, 14th International Conference on Interactive Theorem Proving (ITP 2023), pages 13:1-13:18","descriptionType":"SeriesInformation"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.ITP.2023.13","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":1,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":1,"citationsOverTime":[{"year":"2025","total":1}],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2023-07-26T12:46:25.000Z","registered":"2023-07-26T12:46:26.000Z","published":"2023","updated":"2023-12-21T16:01:17.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"lzi.drops","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"lzi","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.4230/lipics.itp.2023.13","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[{"id":"10.4230/lipics.itp.2025.4","type":"dois"}]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[]}}}}